Privacy Policy for DevJSON

Last updated: May 2026

Overview

DevJSON is a lightweight browser extension designed to format, beautify, validate, and explore JSON and XML data directly within your browser.

Your privacy is important to us.

Data Collection

DevJSON does not collect, store, transmit, or share any personal information or user data.

The extension:

Does not track browsing activity
Does not collect analytics
Does not use cookies
Does not send data to external servers
Does not require user accounts or login
Local Processing

All JSON and XML formatting, validation, search, and tree rendering operations are performed entirely locally within your browser.

Your data never leaves your device.

Permissions

DevJSON only requests the minimum permissions necessary for extension functionality.

The extension does not access or modify user data unrelated to its core functionality.

Third-Party Services

DevJSON does not integrate with third-party analytics, advertising, or tracking services.

Security

Because all processing happens locally, your JSON/XML content remains private and secure on your device.

Changes to This Policy

This privacy policy may be updated occasionally to reflect extension improvements or Chrome Web Store policy updates.

Any future changes will be reflected on this page.

